  'Unified platform for identity, access, and device management that enables secure IT for organizations of any size.', 'JumpCloud is a cloud-based directory and identity management platform founded in 2012 and headquartered in Louisville, Colorado. The platform provides unified endpoint management (UEM), single sign-on (SSO), multi-factor authentication (MFA), privileged access management (PAM), and SaaS management in a single interface. JumpCloud serves more than 150,000 organizations including 5,000+ paying customers such as Cars.com, GoFundMe, Grab, ClassPass, and Peloton. The company became a unicorn in 2021 after raising over $400 million in funding.', 'https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=jumpcloud.com&sz=256',
  2012, '500+', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/jumpcloud', 'https://twitter.com/JumpCloud', 'https://www.facebook.com/JumpCloud.DaaS',
  'company', 0, '["Identity Management","Unified Endpoint Management","SSO and MFA","Zero Trust IT"]', '["Technology","Financial Services","Healthcare","Education","Nonprofit","Retail","Manufacturing"]', '["English"]', NULL, '[{"question":"What is JumpCloud used for?","answer":"JumpCloud is used to centrally manage user identities, device access, single sign-on, multi-factor authentication, and endpoint security across an organization''s entire IT environment."},{"question":"Does JumpCloud replace Active Directory?","answer":"JumpCloud serves as a cloud-based alternative or complement to Microsoft Active Directory, offering directory services, SSO, and device management without requiring on-premises infrastructure."},{"question":"How many companies use JumpCloud?","answer":"JumpCloud serves more than 150,000 organizations worldwide, including over 5,000 paying customers as of 2026."},{"question":"Is JumpCloud suitable for small businesses?","answer":"Yes, JumpCloud is specifically designed to bring enterprise-grade identity and device management to small and mid-sized organizations without requiring a large IT team."},{"question":"When was JumpCloud founded?","answer":"JumpCloud was founded in 2012 in Louisville, Colorado, by Rajat Bhargava and co-founders, and formally launched at TechCrunch Disrupt in 2013."}]',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["GMT-07:00 (Mountain)"]',
  '[{"name":"Identity and Access Management (SSO, MFA, PAM)","percentage":40},{"name":"Unified Endpoint Management (UEM, MDM)","percentage":30},{"name":"Cloud Directory and Lifecycle Management","percentage":20},{"name":"SaaS Management and Discovery","percentage":10}]', '[{"name":"SMB","percentage":45},{"name":"Mid-Market","percentage":40},{"name":"Enterprise","percentage":15}]', '[{"name":"Cars.com","website":"https://www.cars.com"},{"name":"GoFundMe","website":"https://www.gofundme.com"},{"name":"Peloton","website":"https://www.onepeloton.com"}]', 'JumpCloud serves 150,000+ organizations globally, including 5,000+ paying customers such as Cars.com, GoFundMe, Grab, ClassPass, and Peloton.',
