  'AI-powered cloud accounting and financial management software built for mid-market organizations and multi-entity businesses.', 'Sage Intacct is a cloud-based accounting and financial management software platform founded in 1999 and headquartered in San Jose, California. Acquired by The Sage Group for $850 million in 2017, it is now a core product in Sage''s portfolio. The platform serves mid-market organizations in nonprofit, professional services, healthcare, SaaS, construction, and financial services with modules for general ledger, accounts payable and receivable, project accounting, subscription billing, and multi-entity consolidations. Sage Intacct is the AICPA-preferred financial management solution and ranked the top US nonprofit finance system.', 'https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=sageintacct.com&sz=256',
  1999, '500+', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/sageintacct', 'https://twitter.com/SageIntacct', NULL,
  'company', 0, '["Cloud Accounting","Financial Management","Multi-Entity Consolidation","Nonprofit Accounting"]', '["Nonprofit","Professional Services","Healthcare","Financial Services","Construction","SaaS and Subscription","Hospitality","Distribution","Government"]', '["English"]', NULL, '[{"question":"Who owns Sage Intacct?","answer":"Sage Intacct is a subsidiary of The Sage Group plc, a publicly listed UK software company that acquired Sage Intacct in 2017 for $850 million."},{"question":"What industries does Sage Intacct specialize in?","answer":"Sage Intacct has deep functionality for nonprofits, professional services, healthcare, SaaS businesses, construction, financial services, and multi-location hospitality organizations."},{"question":"Is Sage Intacct better than QuickBooks for mid-market companies?","answer":"Sage Intacct is designed for organizations that have outgrown QuickBooks, offering multi-entity consolidation, project accounting, subscription billing, and advanced reporting that QuickBooks does not natively support."},{"question":"Does Sage Intacct integrate with Salesforce?","answer":"Yes, Sage Intacct has a native, certified integration with Salesforce CRM, as well as integrations with ADP, SAP Concur, and hundreds of other business applications."},{"question":"When was Sage Intacct founded?","answer":"Sage Intacct was founded in 1999 in San Jose, California, and operated independently before being acquired by The Sage Group in 2017."}]',
  NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["GMT-08:00 (Pacific)"]',
