  'company', 0, '["Architecture","Healthcare Design","Sustainable Design","Education","Urban Planning"]', '["Healthcare","Science and Technology","Education","Commercial Workplace","Government","Sports and Recreation","Residential","Transportation"]', '["English"]', '[{"name":"Interior Design Sustainability Giant","year":2024},{"name":"Architizer Best Sustainable Firm","year":2023},{"name":"Metropolis Firm of the Year","year":2022},{"name":"Texas Society of Architects Architecture Firm Award - Dallas Studio","year":2024}]', '[{"question":"What is Perkins and Will known for?","answer":"Perkins and Will is globally recognized for sustainable, evidence-based design across healthcare, science and technology labs, higher education, corporate workplaces, and public sector buildings."},{"question":"How many offices does Perkins and Will operate?","answer":"The firm operates design studios in 24 cities across six continents, including offices in Chicago, New York, London, Vancouver, and Copenhagen."},{"question":"What sustainability credentials does Perkins and Will hold?","answer":"Perkins and Will is consistently ranked among the world''s most sustainable design firms. They integrate LEED, WELL, and other certification frameworks into projects and conduct original research to advance climate action in the built environment."},{"question":"Does Perkins and Will work on healthcare projects?","answer":"Yes. Healthcare is one of the firm''s core practice areas. Recent projects include UT Southwestern''s New Pediatric Campus, which won the Gold Touchstone Award from the Center for Health Design for evidence-based design."}]',
