  'One of the world''s largest professional services firms, delivering transformative infrastructure and environmental solutions in 50 countries.', 'WSP Global traces its origins to 1959 and has grown through major acquisitions - including Parsons Brinckerhoff (2014), Golder Associates (2020), and TRC Companies (2026) - into a firm of 83,000 employees operating across approximately 500 offices in 50 countries. Listed on the Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: WSP) and part of the S&P/TSX 60, the company reported revenues of C$16.17 billion in 2024. WSP provides consulting across transportation, buildings, environment, energy, water, and advisory services, and was named to the S&P Global Sustainability Yearbook 2024.', 'https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsp.com&sz=256',
