  'A global advisory, broking, and solutions company helping organisations improve performance through effective risk and people management.', 'Willis Towers Watson (WTW) was formed in January 2016 through the merger of Willis Group and Towers Watson, tracing roots to Henry Willis and Co. founded in the 1840s. The company employs approximately 48,900 people and reported revenue of $9.93 billion in 2024. WTW operates through two segments - Health, Wealth and Career (59% of revenue) and Risk and Broking (41%) - serving the majority of Fortune 1000 companies with employee benefits consulting, actuarial services, risk advisory, and insurance broking. The firm is listed on NASDAQ (WTW) and included in the S&P 500.', 'https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wtwco.com&sz=256',
