  'A top-15 U.S. accounting and advisory firm serving middle-market and entrepreneurial businesses - now part of CBIZ following a 2024 acquisition.', 'Marcum LLP was founded in 1951 and grew to become one of the largest independent accounting firms in the U.S., serving middle-market and entrepreneurial companies, nonprofits, and high net worth individuals from 43 offices nationwide. In November 2024, CBIZ completed a $2.3 billion acquisition of Marcum, with the attest business transferred to Mayer Hoffman McCann. The combined CBIZ-Marcum entity became the largest full-service professional services advisor of its kind in the U.S. with approximately $2.8 billion in combined annualized revenue. Marcum had approximately 3,500 professionals and ranked 13th among U.S. accounting firms prior to the acquisition.', 'https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=marcumllp.com&sz=256',
  1951, '500+', 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/marcum-llp', 'https://x.com/MarcumLLP', NULL,
  'company', 0, '["Audit and Assurance","Tax","Advisory","Middle Market","Accounting"]', '["Technology","Financial Services","Real Estate","Healthcare","Nonprofit","Manufacturing","Construction","Private Equity"]', '["English"]', NULL, '[{"question":"Is Marcum LLP still independent?","answer":"No. In November 2024, CBIZ completed a $2.3 billion acquisition of Marcum. The non-attest business was acquired by CBIZ, while the attest business was transferred to Mayer Hoffman McCann (MHM). The combined CBIZ-Marcum entity is now the largest full-service professional services advisor of its kind in the U.S."},{"question":"What services did Marcum provide?","answer":"Marcum offered a full spectrum of audit and assurance, tax, advisory, technology solutions, and executive search services, with deep expertise serving middle-market, entrepreneurial, and private equity-backed businesses."},{"question":"What industries did Marcum focus on?","answer":"Marcum had dedicated practices in technology, real estate, financial services, healthcare, nonprofit, manufacturing, construction, and private equity portfolio companies."},{"question":"How large was Marcum before the CBIZ merger?","answer":"Prior to the November 2024 acquisition, Marcum had approximately 3,500 professionals across 43 U.S. offices and approximately $1.2 billion in annual revenue, ranking 13th among U.S. accounting firms."}]',
